{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q410634","formula":"C₄H₂O₄","hill":"C4H2O4","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":2.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Acetylenedicarboxylic acid","ru":"Ацетилендикарбоновая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Acetylenedicarboxylic acid or butynedioic acid is an organic compound (a dicarboxylic acid) with the formula H2C4O4 or HO−C(=O)−C≡C−C(=O)−OH. It is a crystalline solid that is soluble in diethyl ether. The removal of two protons yields the acetylenedicarboxylate dianion C4O2−4, which consists only of carbon and oxygen, making it an oxocarbon anion. Partial ionization yields the monovalent hydrogen acetylenedicarboxylate anion HC4O−4.","ru":"Ацетилендикарбоновая кислота (бутиндиовая кислота) — двухосновная непредельная карбоновая кислота с химической формулой HOOC-С≡С-COOH. Представляет собой бесцветные кристаллы, которые хорошо растворяются в воде, этаноле, эфире."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":371,"mass":114.06,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(#CC(=O)O)C(=O)O","inchikey":"YTIVTFGABIZHHX-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"but-2-ynedioic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"371","atoms":10,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.614,"y":-1.043,"z":-0.546,"el":"O"},{"x":2.588,"y":1.049,"z":-0.548,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.648,"y":0.987,"z":0.504,"el":"O"},{"x":2.664,"y":-0.984,"z":0.499,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.037,"y":0.045,"z":0.024,"el":"C"},{"x":2.04,"y":-0.048,"z":0.023,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.597,"y":0.01,"z":0.023,"el":"C"},{"x":0.603,"y":-0.016,"z":0.022,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.594,"y":-0.988,"z":-0.529,"el":"H"},{"x":3.569,"y":1.016,"z":-0.542,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[0,8,1],[1,5,1],[1,9,1],[2,4,2],[3,5,2],[4,6,1],[5,7,1],[6,7,3]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q410634","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"descrip